{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"1st state\">\n  <state id=\"1st state\"><transition event=\"go\" target=\"done\"/></state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":3,"notes":0,"total":3,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":74,"endLine":1,"startColumn":71,"startLine":1}}}],"message":{"markdown":"initial state `1st` does not exist\n\n**Note:** ID references are whitespace-separated lists, so `1st state` is read as separate IDs; the root cause is the invalid ID declaration (SCXML003)\n\n**Help:** rename the declaration to a valid NCName and update this reference; the SCXML003 suggestion does both\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"initial state `1st` does not exist"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":73,"start":70},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"declared here as a single ID containing whitespace"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":23,"endLine":2,"startColumn":14,"startLine":2}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML006"},{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":80,"endLine":1,"startColumn":75,"startLine":1}}}],"message":{"markdown":"initial state `state` does not exist\n\n**Note:** ID references are whitespace-separated lists, so `1st state` is read as separate IDs; the root cause is the invalid ID declaration (SCXML003)\n\n**Help:** rename the declaration to a valid NCName and update this reference; the SCXML003 suggestion does both\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"initial state `state` does not exist"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":79,"start":74},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"declared here as a single ID containing whitespace"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":23,"endLine":2,"startColumn":14,"startLine":2}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML006"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":9,"byteOffset":70,"endColumn":80,"endLine":1,"startColumn":71,"startLine":1},"insertedContent":{"text":"_1st_state"}},{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":9,"byteOffset":95,"endColumn":23,"endLine":2,"startColumn":14,"startLine":2},"insertedContent":{"text":"_1st_state"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename to the valid NCName `_1st_state` and update its reference"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":23,"endLine":2,"startColumn":14,"startLine":2}}}],"message":{"markdown":"identifier `1st state` is not an XML NCName\n\n**Note:** SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`\n\n**Help:** start with a letter or underscore and use only NCName characters; colons are not allowed\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"identifier `1st state` is not an XML NCName"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":104,"start":95},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"referenced here"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml003-invalid-ncname-references.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":80,"endLine":1,"startColumn":71,"startLine":1}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML003"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML IDs are XML IDs: they must start with a letter or `_` and contain only NCName characters (no spaces or colons), so references can be tokenized unambiguously. An `id` is `xsd:ID`, whose white space collapses (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), so leading and trailing white space is not part of it: `id=\" s \"` declares `s`"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: rename the identifier to a valid NCName, for example replacing spaces and colons with `_`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML003` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#IDs","id":"SCXML003","name":"SCXML003","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an identifier is not an XML NCName"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"the `initial` attribute of `<scxml>` or `<state>` selects the states entered first; an unknown ID, or an empty list, leaves the initial configuration undefined"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: correct the identifier or declare the missing state; omit an empty `initial` to enter the first child state.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.2 <scxml>\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML006` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#scxml","id":"SCXML006","name":"SCXML006","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an `initial` attribute names a state that does not exist"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}